# The shell scripts of this project are executed on Linux, as they are: a
# carriage return at the end of a shebang line makes the kernel look for an
# interpreter called "/bin/sh\r" and refuse to run the file at all, and a
# carriage return at the end of a line in the crontab ends up inside the URL
# that curl is asked to fetch. A checkout on Windows writes them that way
# unless it is told not to, which is what this file is for.
*.sh text eol=lf
containers/cron/cron_tasks text eol=lf
